# MiSTerPlex settings → /media/fat/linux/misterplex.conf
#
# BOOT_NET_ADDR (exact key). scripts/misterplexd-boot.sh and
# scripts/misterplexd-boot-mast.sh wait for this IPv4 on BOOT_NET_IF (eth0
# unless set). Env BOOT_NET_ADDR overrides this line. If both are unset the
# address wait is skipped and the daemon still starts. This template does not
# bake an address. Lab card fragments are not part of the public source tree.
# BOOT_NET_ADDR=192.0.2.20
#
# FRIENDLY_NAME and PLAYER_ID (exact keys). Env BOOT_NAME / FRIENDLY_NAME and
# BOOT_ID / PLAYER_ID / MPX_ID override them. When name and id are both unset,
# the boot scripts derive misterplex- plus the last three octets of the IPv4
# at runtime (192.0.2.20 -> misterplex-0.2.20).
# FRIENDLY_NAME=
# PLAYER_ID=
# After edits, reboot, or:
#   /media/fat/misterplex/bin/misterplexd-boot-rc3.sh stop
#   /media/fat/misterplex/bin/misterplexd-boot-rc3.sh start
# Do not use killall. The program ignores SIGTERM.

# Fallback core prefix. The program pins this value; a different line is ignored.
MPX_LEGACY_CORE_PREFIX=999800cf

# --- PMS (multi-server) ---
# Default / fallback base (first in list). Cast playMedia address= still wins when present.
# Set this to your Plex Media Server, for example:
# PLEX_BASE=http://YOUR-PLEX-SERVER:32400
# Optional: comma-separated additional servers (or use multiple PLEX_BASE= lines).
# PLEX_SERVERS=http://SERVER-A:32400,http://SERVER-B:32400
# PLEX_BASE=http://ANOTHER-PLEX-SERVER:32400
# PLEX_HOST=YOUR-PLEX-SERVER
# Optional static token (cast often supplies transient X-Plex-Token)
# PLEX_TOKEN=

# Optional AirPlay helper on another computer. Leave unset to use the
# on-card helper at 127.0.0.1:18781. 192.0.2.10 is a documentation example.
# AIRPLAY_XCODE=http://192.0.2.10:18780
# GCAST_XCODE is the old name for AIRPLAY_XCODE. An existing GCAST_XCODE= line
# still works when AIRPLAY_XCODE is unset.
# AIRPLAY_MIRROR=1 opts in to screen mirroring (SETUP type 110) and the FPGA
# feed. Default off: unset does not advertise mirroring. A card that mirrors
# sets 1. Env AIRPLAY_MIRROR overrides this line.
# AIRPLAY_MIRROR=0

# --- PlexOB direct play -------------------------------------------------------
# A new card turns the Tip A switches on (the set below, plus soft subtitles
# and the Program-menu Subtitles row). Delete a line to leave that switch off.
# Subtitle burn stays off.
# ALLOW_480P60=1 lets a source at or under 854x480 and at most 60 fps direct-play
# (the PlexOB core can do 480p60). Default off: the client profile caps frame
# rate at 30, so 60 fps is transcoded. 720p60 and anything wider than 854 stay
# transcoded either way. 1280x720, 8-bit, bitrate, and H.264 caps still apply.
# Env MPX_ALLOW_480P60 or ALLOW_480P60 overrides this line.
ALLOW_480P60=1

# PAUSE_DIM=1 scales painted OSD/UI RGB to about 40% while playback is paused,
# and after PAUSE_DIM_IDLE_MIN minutes (default 5) on a still PlexUI, library
# page, or menu. Resume, play, or a new UI frame restores full brightness.
# Default off: the pause bar matches the build without this flag. The FPGA
# picture is not scaled. Env MPX_PAUSE_DIM or PAUSE_DIM overrides this line.
PAUSE_DIM=1
# PAUSE_DIM_IDLE_MIN=5

# YT_NEXT_PREV=1 honors YouTube lounge next/previous (skip within the queue).
# Default off: those commands stay ignored. A video that ends still advances
# the queue. Play, pause, seek, and stop are unchanged either way.
# Env MPX_YT_NEXT_PREV or YT_NEXT_PREV overrides this line.
YT_NEXT_PREV=1

# YT_LIVE=1 casts a YouTube livestream (and a premiere that has started) by
# copy-remuxing its HLS manifest to MPEG-TS with the on-card helper ffmpeg.
# The player opens 127.0.0.1, not the manifest. Default off: a VOD cast uses
# the https selector and the googlevideo URL, as before. Needs local yt-dlp
# and /media/fat/misterplex/bin/ffmpeg. A healthy remote AIRPLAY_XCODE still
# takes YouTube through that helper, which is VOD-only.
# Env MPX_YT_LIVE or YT_LIVE overrides this line.
# YT_LIVE=0

# YT_VOLUME=1 honors YouTube lounge setVolume / getVolume. setVolume with an
# integer 0-100 calls the player setVolumePercent, and the phone gets
# onVolumeChanged at that level. getVolume replies the last applied level
# (100 until a set). Default off: both commands still reply onVolumeChanged
# 100 and the player volume is unchanged.
# Env MPX_YT_VOLUME or YT_VOLUME overrides this line.
YT_VOLUME=1

# YT_CAST_TITLE=1 shows the YouTube video title on the play bar and the phone
# now-playing line. The title is the one the local yt-dlp resolve already
# extracted (player videoDetails.title). That resolve does not request
# captions. Default off: the OSD title is unchanged.
# Env MPX_YT_CAST_TITLE or YT_CAST_TITLE overrides this line.
YT_CAST_TITLE=1

# Persistent yt-dlp cache on writable SD (the root filesystem is read-only).
# Env MPX_YT_CACHE_DIR overrides this line.
# YT_CACHE_DIR=/media/fat/misterplex/yt-cache

# Resident stdlib Python 3.9+ Android resolver, only while PlexOB/legacy Plex is
# open (never Spelunkr). Default on; startup is async and an unready/failed
# helper immediately falls back to one-shot yt-dlp with the SD cache above.
# Worker runs nice 10, capped at 96 MiB RSS, with 1-60s crash respawn backoff.
# MPX_YT_WARM / MPX_YT_WARM_SOCK / MPX_YT_WARM_SCRIPT env override these keys.
# YT_WARM=0
# YT_WARM_SOCK=/media/fat/misterplex/yt-warm.sock
# YT_WARM_SCRIPT=/media/fat/misterplex/yt_warm_helper.py
# Socket/endpoint marker, .lock and .log stay on SD. vfat uses an abstract
# AF_UNIX address named by YT_WARM_SOCK plus a small "abstract" marker on SD.
# Deploy/restart inhibition: MPX_DEPLOYING=1, /tmp/misterplex-deploy.lock,
# /tmp/misterplex-restart.lock, /tmp/misterplexd-boot.lock.d, or a held flock
# on /media/fat/misterplex/run/candidate-deploy.lock stops/blocks the helper.
# Scripts without a lock must create /tmp/misterplex-deploy.lock before work
# and remove it afterward. No generic deploy lock currently exists.

# Whole YouTube resolve ladder budget in seconds (10-120, default 90).
# Android first avoids JS-player work without deno/node; other clients fall back
# within the same budget. Env MPX_YT_RESOLVE_TIMEOUT overrides this line.
# YT_RESOLVE_TIMEOUT=90

# YT_CAPTIONS=1 shows YouTube lounge captions on the HDMI caption band.
# setSubtitlesTrack with a language asks the local yt-dlp (the same binary as
# playback) to write that subtitle, then paints it in time with the picture.
# An empty track hides it. getSubtitlesTrack tells the phone which language
# is on. Default off: setSubtitlesTrack is ignored, getSubtitlesTrack still
# replies with the video id only, and no caption text is painted. SOFT_SUBS
# is a separate switch and is not required.
# Env MPX_YT_CAPTIONS or YT_CAPTIONS overrides this line.
# YT_CAPTIONS=0

# MARK_WATCHED=1 adds program-menu rows for the playing item, and for the
# focused movie or episode while browsing: Mark watched, Mark unwatched, and
# Remove from Continue Watching. Those call PMS /:/scrobble, /:/unscrobble, and
# PUT /actions/removeFromContinueWatching. Playback progress still uses
# /:/timeline. Default off: the menu matches a build without this flag.
# Env MPX_MARK_WATCHED or MARK_WATCHED overrides this line.
# MARK_WATCHED=0

# REPORT_CODE=1 shows a short code on the Ready card and the phone status
# page, and writes a redacted log pack under /media/fat/misterplex/reports/.
# The code is the file name. Nothing is uploaded. Default off: the card and
# the page match a build without this flag. Unset is off.
# Env MPX_REPORT_CODE or REPORT_CODE overrides this line.
REPORT_CODE=1

# AMBIENT=1 cycles library art on the idle screen (the OwenB Ready card stays
# on top). Art comes from this server's recently added titles. One title holds;
# two or more change about every 12 seconds. IDLE_SCREEN is unchanged.
# Default off: the idle field stays black and nothing is fetched. Unset is off.
# A stage card that must stay quiet sets this to 0. Env MPX_AMBIENT or AMBIENT overrides this line.
AMBIENT=1

# THEME_MUSIC=1 plays a short generated pad on the plexui Home screen while
# nothing is playing (GH#193 / #235). Uses the one-shot MrAudio path. Default
# off: unset is off. Env MPX_THEME_MUSIC or THEME_MUSIC overrides this line.
# THEME_MUSIC=0

# ZAPAROO=1 plays a Plex movie or episode when a card text hits
# GET or POST /misterplex/zaparoo?text=<card>. The card is a Zaparoo
# launcher token (**launch.plex:/library/metadata/<ratingKey>), a plex:
# URI, a /library/metadata/<ratingKey> path, or the ratingKey alone.
# Playback is the cast play path on this card's PMS. Default off: the
# route answers "zaparoo off" and does not play. Unset is off.
# A stage card that must stay quiet sets this to 0. Env MPX_ZAPAROO or ZAPAROO overrides this line.
ZAPAROO=1

# FILTER_4_3=1 adds a "4:3" chip on the library grid, after All. Select
# hides titles whose aspectRatio is outside 1.30–1.40 (4:3 and academy).
# Select again shows the full grid. Missing aspect is hidden while the
# filter is on. Default off: there is no chip and the grid is unchanged.
# Unset is off. A stage card that must stay quiet sets this to 0.
# Env MPX_FILTER_4_3 or FILTER_4_3 overrides this line.
FILTER_4_3=1

# IN_PLAY_OPTIONS=1 adds Options to the Program menu while a title is
# playing. The page shows the open picture size and Play from start, which
# seeks to the beginning. Default off: the menu matches a build without
# this flag and nothing seeks to 0 from this path. Unset is off.
# A stage card that must stay quiet sets this to 0.
# Env MPX_IN_PLAY_OPTIONS or IN_PLAY_OPTIONS overrides this line.
IN_PLAY_OPTIONS=1

# WATCHED_BADGES=1 draws an orange check on the top-right of a poster whose
# title is finished (viewCount > 0 and no in-progress viewOffset). Library
# grids, home rows, seasons, episodes, and the detail poster use it. An
# in-progress title keeps its progress bar and does not get the check.
# Default off: posters match a build without this flag. Unset is off.
# A stage card that must stay quiet sets this to 0.
# Env MPX_WATCHED_BADGES or WATCHED_BADGES overrides this line.
WATCHED_BADGES=1

# CRT_LOOK=1 paints an HDMI CRT-look preset on the on-device UI canvas
# (home, library, detail). The FPGA picture and the analog raster are
# unchanged. CRT_LOOK_PRESET is scanlines (default), scanlines-soft,
# aperture, or slot. See docs/crt-look-hdmi.md. Default off: the canvas
# matches a build without this flag. Unset is off.
# A stage card that must stay quiet sets this to 0.
# Env MPX_CRT_LOOK or CRT_LOOK overrides this line.
# Env MPX_CRT_LOOK_PRESET or CRT_LOOK_PRESET overrides the preset line.
CRT_LOOK=1
# CRT_LOOK_PRESET=scanlines

# IDLE_MENU_KEY=1 maps USB keyboard P (PS/2 set-2 make code 0x4D) to the
# Program menu on the Ready idle screen, the same panel as pad Y (Safe area
# is on that panel). M, Tab, and F12 are unchanged: on Ready idle with a
# library they still open Browse. In a play, P does nothing (pad Y still
# skips back). In PlexUI, P does nothing (pad Y still toggles UI size).
# Default off: P is not a key. Unset is off. A stage card that must stay quiet sets this to 0.
# Env MPX_IDLE_MENU_KEY or IDLE_MENU_KEY overrides this line.
IDLE_MENU_KEY=1

# GRID_PAGE=1 lets a library grid load titles past the first 200. Moving down
# past the last loaded row requests the next page (X-Plex-Container-Start).
# The same applies to a genre filter. Default off: the grid is the first page
# only, as before. Search and collections are unchanged.
# Env MPX_GRID_PAGE or GRID_PAGE overrides this line.
# GRID_PAGE=0

# AZ_JUMP=1 lets a library grid jump to titles starting with a letter.
# UP from the category chips opens an A–Z bar. Left and Right move the letter,
# Select loads PMS firstCharacter, Down returns to the chips. * clears the
# letter. # is titles that do not start with A–Z. With GRID_PAGE=1, moving
# past the loaded rows fetches the next page of that letter. Default off: the
# library grid matches a build without this flag.
# Env MPX_AZ_JUMP or AZ_JUMP overrides this line.
# AZ_JUMP=0

# SETSTREAMS=1 lists Subtitles and Audio in the Program menu during a play.
# Subtitles includes Off. Choosing a track reopens the picture at the current
# offset. Image tracks (PGS, VobSub) are burned by PMS (subtitles=burn and
# that subtitleStreamID). Audio sends audioStreamID the same way. Unset is off
# and the Program menu has no Subtitles row. This template sets it on. Plex
# Web setStreams is unchanged. Subtitle burn (BURN_SUBS_FIX / AUTO_BURN) stays off.
# Env MPX_SETSTREAMS or SETSTREAMS overrides this line.
SETSTREAMS=1

# CHAPTERS=1 lists Previous chapter, Next chapter, and Chapters in the Program
# menu during a play that has PMS chapter markers. A row seeks to that marker's
# startTimeOffset. The metadata GET adds includeChapters=1 only when this is
# on. Default off: that GET and the menu match a build without this flag.
# Env MPX_CHAPTERS or CHAPTERS overrides this line. Unset is off.
CHAPTERS=1

# FORCED_SUBS=1 selects a PMS subtitle stream marked forced=1 on play and on
# re-resolve when you did not pick a track. Soft text uses the overlay. Image
# tracks (PGS, VobSub) are burned by PMS, the same path as an explicit image
# pick. This is not SUBTITLE_FORCED (that one only keeps forced tracks when
# SUBTITLE_LANG matches). Default off: the pick matches a build without this flag.
# Env MPX_FORCED_SUBS or FORCED_SUBS overrides this line. Unset is off.
FORCED_SUBS=1

# REMEMBER_TRACKS=1 stores the subtitle and audio you pick in the Program menu
# or via setStreams. The file is remember_tracks.txt next to this conf, keyed
# by the show (episode grandparentRatingKey, otherwise ratingKey). The next
# episode uses that subtitleStreamID and audioStreamID when the file still has
# them, otherwise the stream with the same language, codec, and title. Image
# tracks (PGS, VobSub) burn on the explicit-image path. Subtitles Off stays
# off. Unset is off. Picture 14:9 stays the per-play PICTURE_14_9 toggle.
# Env MPX_REMEMBER_TRACKS or REMEMBER_TRACKS overrides this line.
REMEMBER_TRACKS=1

# REMEMBER_PICTURE=1 stores the Program-menu picture mode for the show
# (episode grandparentRatingKey, otherwise ratingKey) in remember_picture.txt
# next to this conf. The row cycles Letterbox, 14:9, Zoom 4:3, Stretch, and
# Fit-crop, the modes the PlexOB core already applies (Analog Aspect Fit /
# Letterbox / Crop, Aspect Ratio 4:3 or 16:9, and the 14:9 side crop). The
# next episode of that show starts in the saved mode. A show with no row is
# unchanged. Unset is off: no row, no file write, and the picture matches a
# build without this flag. The core's own menu is still restored at the end
# of the play.
# Env MPX_REMEMBER_PICTURE or REMEMBER_PICTURE overrides this line. Unset is off.
REMEMBER_PICTURE=1

# SCRUB_THUMBS=1 shows a Plex preview frame above the seek bar while a seek
# settles. The frame comes from the part's sd BIF (hd if that is the only
# index) at /library/parts/{id}/indexes/{sd|hd}. PMS returns 404 if that path
# ends in .bif. A part with no indexes attribute seeks as usual and does not
# fetch. Unset is off: no fetch, and the bar matches a build without this
# flag. The preview stays up for about four seconds so it can be read on a
# 480i tube.
# Env MPX_SCRUB_THUMBS or SCRUB_THUMBS overrides this line. Unset is off.
SCRUB_THUMBS=1

# --- Legacy Plex.rbf only (not used by PlexOB) ---
# PlexOB does not use an SDRAM board. The DECODE / TRANSCODE_PROFILE settings
# below are for the fallback Plex.rbf core. Leave them unless you are on that core.
# For 240p analog output on PlexOB, use ANALOG_RASTER=240p (see below).

# --- Decode / present (Phase 2 transitional ARM path) ---
# Optional external ffmpeg for legacy subprocess paths. Playback uses libav
# inside misterplexd. This package does not ship a standalone ffmpeg program.
# FFMPEG=
# DECODE bank size when OSD_CONTROL=0 (or before first OSD sample). Product tiers:
#   320x240 (240p), 640x480 (480p bank / 624 coded), 1280x720 (720p).
# With OSD_CONTROL=1 the core menu O[5:4] (240p/480p/720p) wins per play and can
# live-retarget the PMS weak ladder mid-session (stop → re-resolve → resume).
DECODE=1280x720
# PMS universal transcode profile names match product labels:
# TRANSCODE_PROFILE=240p   # 320x240 baseline @1M
# TRANSCODE_PROFILE=480p   # 640x480 baseline @2.5M
# TRANSCODE_PROFILE=720p   # 1280x720 main@L3.1 @20M
TRANSCODE_PROFILE=720p
# Legacy per-field overrides (kept for lab experiments):
# WEAK_RES=1280x720
# WEAK_BITRATE=20000
# PRESENT=fb0|fpga|both — product glass uses fpga (DDR frame store).
PRESENT=fpga
# ANALOG_RASTER=480i|240p|auto — picks the PlexOB core's "Analog Raster" (saved status[24]).
# Unset (default) and auto: no action. 480i/240p act only on the 240p core (build id 0B2403A7), by setting
# that bit in the existing PlexOB_v1.CFG (save settings once in the OSD first) and reloading the core once.
# The daemon writes the readback (word 87 bit 8 requested, bit 9 p240 active) to /tmp/mpx_analog_raster.
# ANALOG_RASTER=
# PRESENT_MEM is a fallback-core memory policy. PlexOB uses DDRAM only and
# does not need an SDRAM board. On PlexOB, 240p analog output is ANALOG_RASTER=240p.
# PRESENT_MEM=auto
# STREAM=1  # annex-B → host I-recon F1 + F3 (Phase 3.3i product path)
# Prefer direct H.264 Part when STREAM=1 (avoids High/CABAC universal for recon).
# High/CABAC: sticky skip from PPS entropy flag (no residual walk per IDR).
# STREAM_SKIP_RGB=auto  # skip heavy RGB only when PRESENT=fpga (audio + recon from start)
# STREAM_SKIP_RGB=0     # always FFmpeg RGB (CABAC fallback / PRESENT=both keeps RGB anyway)
# PRESENT=both always keeps FFmpeg RGB for continuous fb0 regardless of STREAM_SKIP_RGB.

# --- Phase 4 UX ---
# AUTO_NEXT=1  # on media EOF, play next playQueue item when bound (default on)
# AUTO_NEXT=0
# Subtitles: off | burn (PMS universal) | ffmpeg (local files, STREAM=0 only)
# See docs/subtitles-burnin.md
SUBTITLES=off
# SUBTITLE_STREAM=0
# Per-show audio and subtitle choices are stored in show_tracks.txt next to this
# file and applied on later episodes of that show. They stay on this daemon.
# track_pref_server_sync=1 also PUTs /library/parts/{id} so PMS stores the part
# default. That PUT is a persistent manual pick for the Plex user and turns off
# their auto-select for that item in every Plex app, not only MiSTerPlex.
# Default 0: local show prefs still apply, and no PUT is sent.
track_pref_server_sync=0

# --- CRT title-safe / UI size (GH#46) ---
# Percent of each raster axis, clamped 0-15. Default 5 keeps the historic
# PlexUI R1 insets (32/72) so existing goldens stay. Ready/status cards and
# the daemon caption band use the same floor.
# UI_SAFE_MARGIN=5
# UI_SIZE=normal is the safe default (or large). Pad Y on the browse screen
# toggles and persists. A card may set large; this template stays normal.
UI_SAFE_MARGIN=5
UI_SIZE=normal
# Per-tube overscan (Program menu → Safe area). Unset keeps the fixed title-safe.
# Percent of that axis, 0-25. A save writes all four.
OVERSCAN_LEFT=11
OVERSCAN_RIGHT=11
OVERSCAN_TOP=12
OVERSCAN_BOTTOM=12
# 14:9 picture mode for a wide title on a 4:3 tube (Program menu → Picture).
# Unset keeps Fit / Letterbox / Crop. On narrows the SPS window to 14:9 and
# uses the core's existing Letterbox fit. MPX_PICTURE_14_9 wins when set.
PICTURE_14_9=on

# --- Match source Hz / Content FPS (Phase 4) ---
# Plex.rbf does NOT yet implement Groovy-style CmdSwitchres modeline swaps.
# On each play, misterplexd reads PMS videoFrameRate/frameRate and logs a Content
# FPS hint (12/24/30/60). Set OSD **Content FPS** to match for 3:2 / 2:2 cadence.
# SOURCE_FPS=auto → use PMS metadata; 24|30|60|12 forces; off disables hint.
# MATCH_SOURCE_HZ=on logs target Hz but still uses cadence (switchres TODO).
# See docs/match-source-hz.md.
MATCH_SOURCE_HZ=off
SOURCE_FPS=auto

# --- A/V lipsync (post vsync present) ---
# FFmpeg adelay (ms) on the product dual-pipe path. Default 0 = no intentional lag.
# Positive delays audio content vs video (voice-ahead / lips-late → try 20–60 eyes-on).
# Leave AUDIO_DELAY_MS at 0 unless you are measuring lipsync on your own set.
# AUDIO_DELAY_MS=0

# --- A/V pacing (present loop) ---
# Video is paced against the audio master clock using the EXACT content rate parsed
# from PMS (Stream@frameRate), forced into the FFmpeg chain as fps=<num>/<den> so the
# frame index and content time can never diverge. Leave these alone unless measuring.
#
# AV_PRESENT_LEAD_MS: how early a frame may be shown vs the master clock (default 40).
# AV_PRESENT_LEAD_MS=40
#
# AV_RESYNC_DROP_MS: drift past which a late frame is dropped to catch up. 0 disables
# dropping (video then only ever lags on a decode stall). Default 80.
# AV_RESYNC_DROP_MS=80
#
# AV_CONTENT_FPS: override the detected content rate. "auto" (default) uses PMS.
# Accepts "24000/1001", "23.976", "25". Only for debugging bad metadata.
# AV_CONTENT_FPS=auto

# AUDIO_CLOCK_PPM: starting point for the audio feed-rate servo, in ppm off a
# nominal 48 kHz. You should not need to touch this.
#
# /dev/MrAudio is a 512 KB DMA ring with NO backpressure, so any mismatch
# between how fast we feed and how fast the FPGA plays integrates into the ring
# depth forever. The daemon now reads the driver's read pointer and servos the
# feed rate to hold ~100 ms of buffer, so a wrong value here is corrected within
# seconds rather than drifting lipsync all episode.
#
# -638 is the measured clock error of the Plex core (it plays slightly SLOWER
# than nominal). It is only used verbatim as a fallback, if the ring depth
# cannot be read at all.
#
# The previous value here was +685, from an HDMI-capture calibration taken when
# video paced off bytes *submitted*. A ring filling up and a fast playback clock
# are indistinguishable under that clock, so the calibration folded one into the
# other and got the sign wrong.
AUDIO_CLOCK_PPM=-638

# --- Playback input -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# The Plex core publishes keyboard/controller playback commands through a DDR
# mailbox; the daemon polls that mailbox only (no HPS<->FPGA SPI bus access).
# Skip defaults follow common media remote behavior: Right/SkipForward = +30s,
# Left/SkipBack = -10s. Use SKIP_MS to make both directions symmetric, or set
# the directional keys independently.
# SKIP_MS=30000
# SKIP_FORWARD_MS=30000
# SKIP_BACK_MS=10000

# --- OSD menu controls (Plex core CONF_STR v8) --------------------------------
#
# OSD_CONTROL: let the core's OSD menu (F12) drive playback settings live. The
# daemon polls status[15:0] ~4x/s and applies A/V offset, auto-resync, audio
# clock trim, idle screen, and content resolution (O[5:4]: 240p/480p/720p).
# Content-res changes while playing restart the session at the same offset so
# PMS re-encodes to the new weak ladder (no on-device scale when sizes match).
#
# The daemon NEVER writes these bits. Main_MiSTer owns the OSD word and persists
# it to /media/fat/config/Plex_v*.CFG; a daemon-side write fights Main's shadow
# copy and makes the value flap. Read-only polling is the whole contract.
#
# REQUIRES a v3+ Plex.rbf for A/V knobs; content-res 720p rung needs v8 CONF_STR
# (O[5:4]). v7 O[4]-only still maps 240p/480p. Set OSD_CONTROL=0 on pre-v3 cores.
OSD_CONTROL=1
#
# AV_OFFSET_MS: constant audio-vs-video trim applied inside the pacing loop (NOT
# an ffmpeg adelay), so the OSD can change it mid-playback. Positive = present
# video later = audio appears earlier. The OSD exposes -160..+140 ms in 20 ms
# steps; this conf value is the power-on default and is not limited to that grid.
# AV_OFFSET_MS=0
#
# IDLE_SCREEN: what to show when nothing is playing. The FPGA frame store and
# /dev/fb0 both latch the LAST frame written, so without this the final frame of
# the previous video stays on screen forever (a CRT burn-in risk).
#   logo        centred Plex-style chevron on a near-black field (default)
#   black       flat black
#   screensaver chevron drifting slowly to avoid burn-in
#   lastframe   legacy behaviour — leave the last video frame up
# IDLE_SCREEN=logo
#
# MPX_GATE_ERROR_SCREEN: when the FPGA decoder cannot take a stream and no ladder
# helper can play it either, the daemon stops the play and paints the reason
# ("Can't play here: ...") in place of the idle screen until the next play, a
# stop, or a core change.
#   on   paint the reason (default)
#   off  log-only: the play still stops with the same error; nothing is painted
# MPX_GATE_ERROR_SCREEN=on

# --- Library browse (off unless you set both) ---------------------------------
# The helper is a separate program. This package does not include it.
# MPX_BROWSE_V2=1
# Full URL. The path ends at /menu. 192.0.2.10 is a documentation example.
# Point the helper at the same PMS as PLEX_BASE. The /menu list is the server list.
# MPX_MENU_URL=http://192.0.2.10:18769/menu
# Origin only. The daemon appends /menu. Ignored when MPX_MENU_URL is set.
# MPX_MENU_BASE=http://192.0.2.10:18769
# One host for the menu port 18769 when the URL above is unset.
# MPX_LAB_HOST=192.0.2.10
# PLXI nav and the full on-screen plex UI stay off. The Ready-line plex.tv code
# uses PLEXTV_LINK and PLEXTV_TOKEN and does not read MPX_MENU_URL.
# MPX_BROWSE_MVPB=1
# MPX_PLEXUI=1

# --- plex.tv link code --------------------------------------------------------
# PLEXTV_LINK defaults on. An empty PLEXTV_TOKEN starts a PIN exchange and
# appends the code to the idle Ready line. Leave the token empty until sign-in.
# PLEXTV_LINK=1
# PLEXTV_TOKEN=
# Plex Home profile, written by the on-screen Switch user row. Leave these
# unset for a single-user or no-Home account: PLEX_TOKEN and PLEXTV_TOKEN
# stay the library and account tokens. A saved profile is never copied over
# those two keys.
# PLEX_HOME_ID=
# PLEX_HOME_TITLE=
# PLEX_HOME_TOKEN=

# --- TLS (on by default) ------------------------------------------------------
# Plex, PlexUI, YouTube, and the AirPlay helper verify the certificate chain and the hostname.
# The CA bundle is /media/fat/linux/misterplex-cacert.pem (Mozilla roots shipped
# in the release package). The daemon points MPX_CA_BUNDLE at that file when it
# is present and you have not set one. A different bundle:
#   MPX_CA_BUNDLE=/media/fat/linux/misterplex-cacert.pem
#
# Local Plex servers that use plex.direct already match. The certificate is a
# wildcard for *.<id>.plex.direct, and the first label is the LAN address with
# dashes (https://203-0-113-5.<id>.plex.direct:32400). The daemon connects to
# 192.0.2.5 and checks that name. Do not rewrite those URLs to a raw IP before
# TLS; a raw IP is not on the plex.direct certificate.
#
# A server that is genuinely self-signed (or signed by a CA that is not in the
# Mozilla set) needs its PEM next to the bundle, not TLS_VERIFY=0. The file is
# the server certificate or the CA that signed it:
#   TLS_TRUST_FILE=/media/fat/misterplex/trust/pms.pem
#
# TLS_VERIFY=0 turns chain and hostname checks off and logs a warning. Leave it
# unset (or 1) unless a broken server cannot be given a trust file.
# TLS_VERIFY=1

# Phase-1 text subtitles on PlexOB: sidecar SRT/ASS drawn on the overlay band.
# SUBTITLE_LANG=off|en|…  (canon via language names or ISO tags). Empty/off = no auto-lang.
# SUBTITLE_FORCED=1 means forced-only when the language matches.
# FORCED_SUBS (above) is separate: it selects a forced=1 stream on a default play.
# Leave SUBTITLE_FORCED unset unless you want that language filter.
# SUBTITLES=burn is an explicit PMS burn fallback (drops Direct Play). Default off.
# SUBTITLE_STREAM is the old STREAM=0 burn/ffmpeg stream id; leave unset on PlexOB.
# SUBTITLES=off
# SUBTITLE_LANG=off
# SUBTITLE_FORCED=0
# SUBTITLE_STREAM=0
# SUBTITLE_POSITION=safe|picture
# safe (default): when 16:9 or wider picture is letterboxed on a 4:3 raster,
# white soft-sub lines sit in the bottom black bar, inside that bar's
# title-safe area, not over the picture. picture keeps the lines over the
# picture. No letterbox bar: both values use the over-picture placement.
# This is the overlay only. It does not change PMS burn-in.
# SUBTITLE_POSITION=safe

# Soft text from the container (mov_text, WebVTT, embedded SRT/ASS) on the
# overlay band, plus external WebVTT from /library/streams/N. Unset is off:
# sidecar SRT/ASS still paint (fetched on-device from the play's PMS base),
# and mov_text / PGS stay on today's burn path unless SOFT_SUBS=1.
# This template sets SOFT_SUBS=1. MPX_SOFT_SUBS in the environment wins.
SOFT_SUBS=1

# OpenSubtitles.com on-device fallback when a title has no text subtitle stream.
# OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY (or env OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY / MPX_OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY)
# is required. OPENSUBS_FALLBACK defaults on when a key is present; set 0 to skip.
# Optional OPENSUBTITLES_USERNAME / OPENSUBTITLES_PASSWORD for a bearer login. Leave either unset to skip
# /login and download anonymously on the Api-Key alone (5/day per IP; enable "allow anonymous downloads" on
# the key). A 406 (daily limit) backs off for 1 h.
# Cache: /media/fat/misterplex/subs/<ratingKey|imdb>-en.srt. Never log the key.
# OPENSUBTITLES_API_KEY=
# OPENSUBS_FALLBACK=1
# OPENSUBTITLES_USERNAME=
# OPENSUBTITLES_PASSWORD=

# REMOTE_H264_TRANSCODE=1 (#207): every remote Plex play asks the server for an H.264
# transcode that fits the decoder; never a direct source Part on a remote server.
# Default on. Set 0 to keep the original file (HEVC on a friend server then fails).
# Env MPX_REMOTE_H264_TRANSCODE or REMOTE_H264_TRANSCODE overrides this line.
# REMOTE_H264_TRANSCODE=0

# BURN_SUBS_FIX=1 with AUTO_BURN unset is a legacy opt-in: an upgraded box keeps
# burning image subtitles. An explicit AUTO_BURN below wins, including
# AUTO_BURN=0 (burn off even when this key is 1). Neither key set is off.
# When burn is on, BURN_SUBS_FIX=1 forces a video transcode (directPlay=0 /
# directStream=0, and the decision URL carries subtitles=burn) for an image
# subtitle the overlay will not paint (PGS/VobSub). Soft overlay always paints
# SRT/ASS/VTT and does not burn them. Do not set this in a new conf. The
# shipped example leaves it commented. Env MPX_BURN_SUBS_FIX or BURN_SUBS_FIX
# overrides this line.
# BURN_SUBS_FIX=0

# AUTO_BURN is the explicit burn switch. AUTO_BURN=1 burns a picked image
# subtitle the overlay cannot paint (PMS video transcode). AUTO_BURN=0 is off
# and wins over a legacy BURN_SUBS_FIX=1. Unset defers to that legacy key, and
# with neither key set the burn stays off (Direct Play kept). Env
# MPX_AUTO_BURN or AUTO_BURN overrides this line. Same precedence as conf.
# AUTO_BURN=0

# HTTP_RANGE_RESUME=1 (default): a short PMS Part close reopens with
# Range: bytes=<offset>-. HTTP_RANGE_RESUME=0 falls back to libav HTTP.
# Env MPX_HTTP_RANGE_RESUME or HTTP_RANGE_RESUME overrides this line.
# HTTP_RANGE_RESUME=1

# LAN_AUTH=1 requires a LAN shared secret (header X-MPX-Auth) on the
# /misterplex/* control routes and on the transcode helper for non-loopback
# peers. Plex companion routes stay open so the Plex app and Plex Web still
# cast; AirPlay and YouTube go through the daemon, which sends the secret.
# GET /misterplex/status stays open. Default off. Unset is off.
# Secret: LAN_AUTH_SECRET= here, else LAN_AUTH_SECRET_FILE (default
# /media/fat/misterplex/lan_auth.secret, generated on the card; mode 600 is enforced off-FAT,
# relaxed on the FAT/exFAT card where modes are synthetic: ls shows 755 there by design,
# but a mount that makes it group/world-writable is refused; owner must be root or the daemon user (#222)).
# Sender-device test: python3 tools/airplay/lan_auth_sender.py --host <mister-ip>
# Never put a real secret in a shared or STAGE conf. Env MPX_LAN_AUTH wins.
# LAN_AUTH=0
